<title>SINGAPORE: Thai refiner Rayong tenders to sell May gasoline.</title>
<headline>Thai refiner Rayong tenders to sell May gasoline.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thai refiner Rayong Refinery Co Ltd has issued a closed tender to sell around 200,000 barrels of 95-octane unleaded gasoline for loading between May 20-24, sources at the refinery said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The tender will close later on Wednesday afternoon and would be valid until 1700 hours Bangkok time (1000 GMT).</p>
<p>The 145,000 barrels-per-day Rayong refinery 60-percent owned by Shell and 40-percent by state-owned Petroleum Authority if Thailand (PTT).  </p>
<p>In its last tender, the Thai refiner sold 230,000 barrels of 95 octane unleaded gasoline for $1.00 per barrel below Singapore 95-octane quotes to Shell Singapore on a free-on-board basis.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (65-870-3082)</p>
</text>
